WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:02.350
It's 2:07 AM.

2
00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:04.670
A camera in a dealership garage
catches someone

3
00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.170
breaking into an SUV that isn't theirs.

4
00:00:07.833 --> 00:00:11.773
The alarm goes to a monitoring center,
but then it waits in line.

5
00:00:11.813 --> 00:00:13.873
Operators review alarms one at a time,

6
00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:18.511
but most are wind, headlights,
employees, and deliveries.

7
00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:22.510
On a busy night, a real threat
can wait twenty minutes or more.

8
00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:25.270
Monitoring centers just can't
add seats on demand.

9
00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:29.550
Hiring takes months, but spikes
take minutes, so they cut corners.

10
00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:34.670
They mute busy cameras, move operators
offshore, or charge you for extra alarms.

11
00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.871
And during the day,
there's so much activity

12
00:00:37.911 --> 00:00:40.991
that most monitoring companies
don't even offer coverage.

13
00:00:42.266 --> 00:00:45.346
Verdun is the world's
most advanced monitoring center,

14
00:00:45.386 --> 00:00:48.446
where AI agents work
alongside highly trained operators,

15
00:00:48.486 --> 00:00:51.186
so your alarms never
get buried in a queue.

16
00:00:53.137 --> 00:00:54.437
This is a real product.

17
00:00:54.477 --> 00:00:57.197
Agents review every alarm
the moment it fires

18
00:00:57.237 --> 00:00:59.497
and check it against each site's protocol.

19
00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:04.166
People walking through a lot,
dismissed with the reasoning written down.

20
00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:07.190
Someone reaching
into a truck on a dealer lot,

21
00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:10.843
escalated to an operator
in just 16 seconds.

22
00:01:10.883 --> 00:01:12.923
The operator has everything to act:

23
00:01:12.963 --> 00:01:18.453
live video, police dispatch, and a text
to the owner already drafted by the agent.

24
00:01:18.493 --> 00:01:21.873
Every step lands in a complete
timestamped record.

25
00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.330
Verdun covers every camera
around the clock,

26
00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:28.170
including daytime on cameras
that you already have.

27
00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:31.830
Every alarm is reviewed
in under 90 seconds.

28
00:01:32.711 --> 00:01:34.711
I'm Sonny Tai. I'm a former Marine officer

29
00:01:34.751 --> 00:01:37.571
who previously built
a computer vision company for security

30
00:01:37.611 --> 00:01:40.071
that scaled to over 100,000 cameras.

31
00:01:40.111 --> 00:01:43.051
My co-founder, Tung Hoang,
is an applied mathematician

32
00:01:43.091 --> 00:01:47.190
who previously built AI for WeWork,
VergeSense, and LinkedIn.

33
00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:50.951
Together, we built Verdun
so your alarms never wait in line.

34
00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:55.181
Verdun, the next generation
of security monitoring.
